  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Educacin para la Conservacin de la Mariposa Monarca en el Centro de Mxico</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to share the importance, migration phenomena and conservation needs of the monarch butterfly (Danaus plexipus) and other pollinators among key groups across four states from Central Mexico (Aguascalientes, Guanajuato, Jalisco and San Luis Potos). This project is intended to conserve the monarch butterfly by promoting public participation in conservation actions aimed at reducing the loss of migratory feeding grounds in Central Mexico. Specific activities include: (1) the implementation of an environmental education program through educational workshops; (2) the distribution of brochures on the monarch butterflys migration, threats, conservation needs, and on how to build pollinator gardens; (3) building pollinator gardens at hosting institutions; (4) the distribution of field identification guides of the butterflies of Mexico; (5) training and encouraging of participants to document their monarch butterfly sightings on the Naturalista platform of CONABIO; (7) the creation of a monarch butterfly monitoring network for Central Mexico; and (8) hosting the First Meeting of the Monarch Butterfly Monitoring Network of Central Mexico with participating institutions.</narrative>
  </description>
